{"type":"tool_execution_update","toolCallId":"toolu_01J8AfxJe9YThyBWN4Jreaxd","toolName":"bash","args":{"command":"cd /app && git show HEAD:.ki-base/knowledge/_OVERVIEW.ki.md | head -80; git show HEAD:.ki-base/knowledge/KI_rich_null.md | head -30; sed -n 1,60p rich/styled.py"},"partialResult":{"content":[{"type":"text","text":"<!-- last_verified: 2026-11-08 -->\n# _OVERVIEW — Project Overview\n\n**Module**: `rich` (entire project)\n**Last verified**: 2026-11-08\n\n## Overview\n\nRich is a Python library for rendering rich text, tables, syntax highlighting, markdown, progress bars, and formatted data to terminal output and HTML. It serves as the primary rendering engine across console applications to provide modern CLI UX.\n\n## Subsystems & Knowledge Architecture\n\nThe codebase is partitioned into cohesive Knowledge Items (max 10 files per item):\n\n- [[KI_rich_align.md]]: Central `Console` orchestrator, ANSI escape parsing, cells width measurement, borders, and column layouts.\n- [[KI_rich_region.md]]: Low-level rendering primitives: `Segment`, `Style`, `Rule`, `Status`, `Spinner`, and screen switching.\n- [[KI_rich_syntax.md]]: Data presentation components: `Table`, `Text`, `Syntax`, `Traceback`, `Tree`, and `Theme`.\n- [[KI_rich_markdown.md]]: Markdown AST rendering, console `[markup]`, `Panel`, `Pretty` printing, and `Prompt` inputs.\n- [[KI_rich_default.md]]: Proportional multi-pane `Layout`, regex `Highlighter`, `RichHandler` logging, and JSON formatting.\n- [[KI_rich_live.md]]: Dynamic terminal updating (`Live`), multi-task progress meters (`Progress`), and IPython shims.\n- [[KI_rich_emoji.md]]: Emoji parsing, `Color` color models (Standard/256/Truecolor), and Windows console backends.\n- [[KI_rich_null.md]]: Internal ratio math, text wrapping routines, and Win32 low-level structures.\n- [[KI_rich_unicode11-0-0.md]] & [[KI_rich_unicode5-0-0.md]]: Unicode East Asian character width lookup tables.\n\n## Entry Points & Public API\n\n- `rich.print`: Direct drop-in replacement for `print()` with rich markup formatting.\n- `rich.inspect`: Introspective object visualizer.\n- `rich.get_console()`: Global default `Console` instance accessor.\n- `rich.traceback.install()`: Installs Rich exception handler for formatted stack traces.\n\n## Testing & Verification\n\n- Test command: `pytest tests/`\n\n## Architecture Notes\n\n- Follows the Rich Console Protocol (`__rich__` and `__rich_console__`).\n- Renders to atomic `Segment` instances before emitting ANSI escape sequences or Win32 calls.\n- Supports degradation/fallbacks for terminals without 24-bit TrueColor or Windows legacy console environments.\n\n## Related KIs\n\n- [[KI_rich_align.md]]\n- [[KI_rich_region.md]]\n- [[KI_rich_syntax.md]]\n- [[KI_rich_markdown.md]]\n- [[KI_rich_default.md]]\n- [[KI_rich_live.md]]\n- [[KI_rich_emoji.md]]\n- [[KI_rich_null.md]]\n- [[KI_rich_unicode11-0-0.md]]\n- [[KI_rich_unicode5-0-0.md]]\n"}],"details":{}}}
{"type":"tool_execution_update","toolCallId":"toolu_01J8AfxJe9YThyBWN4Jreaxd","toolName":"bash","args":{"command":"cd /app && git show HEAD:.ki-base/knowledge/_OVERVIEW.ki.md | head -80; git show HEAD:.ki-base/knowledge/KI_rich_null.md | head -30; sed -n 1,60p rich/styled.py"},"partialResult":{"content":[{"type":"text","text":"<!-- last_verified: 2026-11-08 -->\n# _OVERVIEW — Project Overview\n\n**Module**: `rich` (entire project)\n**Last verified**: 2026-11-08\n\n## Overview\n\nRich is a Python library for rendering rich text, tables, syntax highlighting, markdown, progress bars, and formatted data to terminal output and HTML. It serves as the primary rendering engine across console applications to provide modern CLI UX.\n\n## Subsystems & Knowledge Architecture\n\nThe codebase is partitioned into cohesive Knowledge Items (max 10 files per item):\n\n- [[KI_rich_align.md]]: Central `Console` orchestrator, ANSI escape parsing, cells width measurement, borders, and column layouts.\n- [[KI_rich_region.md]]: Low-level rendering primitives: `Segment`, `Style`, `Rule`, `Status`, `Spinner`, and screen switching.\n- [[KI_rich_syntax.md]]: Data presentation components: `Table`, `Text`, `Syntax`, `Traceback`, `Tree`, and `Theme`.\n- [[KI_rich_markdown.md]]: Markdown AST rendering, console `[markup]`, `Panel`, `Pretty` printing, and `Prompt` inputs.\n- [[KI_rich_default.md]]: Proportional multi-pane `Layout`, regex `Highlighter`, `RichHandler` logging, and JSON formatting.\n- [[KI_rich_live.md]]: Dynamic terminal updating (`Live`), multi-task progress meters (`Progress`), and IPython shims.\n- [[KI_rich_emoji.md]]: Emoji parsing, `Color` color models (Standard/256/Truecolor), and Windows console backends.\n- [[KI_rich_null.md]]: Internal ratio math, text wrapping routines, and Win32 low-level structures.\n- [[KI_rich_unicode11-0-0.md]] & [[KI_rich_unicode5-0-0.md]]: Unicode East Asian character width lookup tables.\n\n## Entry Points & Public API\n\n- `rich.print`: Direct drop-in replacement for `print()` with rich markup formatting.\n- `rich.inspect`: Introspective object visualizer.\n- `rich.get_console()`: Global default `Console` instance accessor.\n- `rich.traceback.install()`: Installs Rich exception handler for formatted stack traces.\n\n## Testing & Verification\n\n- Test command: `pytest tests/`\n\n## Architecture Notes\n\n- Follows the Rich Console Protocol (`__rich__` and `__rich_console__`).\n- Renders to atomic `Segment` instances before emitting ANSI escape sequences or Win32 calls.\n- Supports degradation/fallbacks for terminals without 24-bit TrueColor or Windows legacy console environments.\n\n## Related KIs\n\n- [[KI_rich_align.md]]\n- [[KI_rich_region.md]]\n- [[KI_rich_syntax.md]]\n- [[KI_rich_markdown.md]]\n- [[KI_rich_default.md]]\n- [[KI_rich_live.md]]\n- [[KI_rich_emoji.md]]\n- [[KI_rich_null.md]]\n- [[KI_rich_unicode11-0-0.md]]\n- [[KI_rich_unicode5-0-0.md]]\n<!-- last_verified: 2026-11-08 -->\n# KI: Rich Core (Internal Utilities & Platform Adaptors)\n\n## Overview\nProvides internal mathematical routines, layout ratio solvers, text wrapping primitives, platform Win32 console structures, and base ABC protocols. It forms the low-level foundation for rendering algorithms.\n\n## Entry Points & Public API\n- `ratio_resolve`: Integer ratio distribution algorithm for flex-like sizing in layouts and tables.\n- `words`: Word wrapping generator yielding split text positions without breaking ANSI tokens.\n- `RichRenderable`: Abstract base class enforcing the `__rich__` rendering protocol.\n- `NullFile`: Dummy writable file descriptor discarding all output.\n\n## Key Components\n| Class / Function | File | Purpose |\n|---|---|---|\n| `ratio_resolve` | `rich/_ratio.py` | Distributes integer space across items according to ratios and constraints |\n| `words` / `divide_line` | `rich/_wrap.py` | Word and character wrapping algorithms respecting cell widths and unicode boundaries |\n| `NullFile` | `rich/_null_file.py` | In-memory dummy stream implementing file protocol methods as no-ops |\n| `Stack` | `rich/_stack.py` | Lightweight wrapper over list providing stack operations with peak inspection |\n| `LegacyWindowsError` / Win32 structs | `rich/_win32_console.py` | ctypes definitions for Win32 Console API handles, buffers, and coordinates |\n| `RichRenderable` | `rich/abc.py` | Abstract base class verifying presence of `__rich__` magic method |\n| `SPINNERS` | `rich/_spinners.py` | Static catalog of animated spinner frame definitions and refresh intervals |\n\n## Testing & Verification\n- Test commands: `pytest tests/test_ratio.py tests/test_null_file.py tests/test_win32_console.py`\n- Test files: `tests/test_ratio.py`, `tests/test_null_file.py`, `tests/test_win32_console.py`\n\n## Non-obvious Details\n- **Integer ratio distribution rounding**: `ratio_resolve` distributes remainder pixels based on largest fractional residuals to ensure sum of parts exactly equals total width.\n- **NullFile compatibility**: Some 3rd-party libraries verify `.isatty()` or `.fileno()`; `NullFile` overrides these to gracefully avoid `io.UnsupportedOperation`.\nfrom typing import TYPE_CHECKING\n\nfrom .measure import Measurement\nfrom .segment import Segment\nfrom .style import StyleType\n\nif TYPE_CHECKING:\n    from .console import Console, ConsoleOptions, RenderResult, RenderableType\n\n\nclass Styled:\n    \"\"\"Apply a style to a renderable.\n\n    Args:\n        renderable (RenderableType): Any renderable.\n        style (StyleType): A style to apply across the entire renderable.\n    \"\"\"\n\n    def __init__(self, renderable: \"RenderableType\", style: \"StyleType\") -> None:\n        self.renderable = renderable\n        self.style = style\n\n    def __rich_console__(\n        self, console: \"Console\", options: \"ConsoleOptions\"\n    ) -> \"RenderResult\":\n        style = console.get_style(self.style)\n        rendered_segments = console.render(self.renderable, options)\n        segments = Segment.apply_style(rendered_segments, style)\n        return segments\n\n    def __rich_measure__(\n        self, console: \"Console\", options: \"ConsoleOptions\"\n    ) -> Measurement:\n        return Measurement.get(console, options, self.renderable)\n\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":  # pragma: no cover\n    from rich import print\n    from rich.panel import Panel\n\n    panel = Styled(Panel(\"hello\"), \"on blue\")\n    print(panel)\n"}],"details":{}}}
{"type":"tool_execution_end","toolCallId":"toolu_01J8AfxJe9YThyBWN4Jreaxd","toolName":"bash","result":{"content":[{"type":"text","text":"<!-- last_verified: 2026-11-08 -->\n# _OVERVIEW — Project Overview\n\n**Module**: `rich` (entire project)\n**Last verified**: 2026-11-08\n\n## Overview\n\nRich is a Python library for rendering rich text, tables, syntax highlighting, markdown, progress bars, and formatted data to terminal output and HTML. It serves as the primary rendering engine across console applications to provide modern CLI UX.\n\n## Subsystems & Knowledge Architecture\n\nThe codebase is partitioned into cohesive Knowledge Items (max 10 files per item):\n\n- [[KI_rich_align.md]]: Central `Console` orchestrator, ANSI escape parsing, cells width measurement, borders, and column layouts.\n- [[KI_rich_region.md]]: Low-level rendering primitives: `Segment`, `Style`, `Rule`, `Status`, `Spinner`, and screen switching.\n- [[KI_rich_syntax.md]]: Data presentation components: `Table`, `Text`, `Syntax`, `Traceback`, `Tree`, and `Theme`.\n- [[KI_rich_markdown.md]]: Markdown AST rendering, console `[markup]`, `Panel`, `Pretty` printing, and `Prompt` inputs.\n- [[KI_rich_default.md]]: Proportional multi-pane `Layout`, regex `Highlighter`, `RichHandler` logging, and JSON formatting.\n- [[KI_rich_live.md]]: Dynamic terminal updating (`Live`), multi-task progress meters (`Progress`), and IPython shims.\n- [[KI_rich_emoji.md]]: Emoji parsing, `Color` color models (Standard/256/Truecolor), and Windows console backends.\n- [[KI_rich_null.md]]: Internal ratio math, text wrapping routines, and Win32 low-level structures.\n- [[KI_rich_unicode11-0-0.md]] & [[KI_rich_unicode5-0-0.md]]: Unicode East Asian character width lookup tables.\n\n## Entry Points & Public API\n\n- `rich.print`: Direct drop-in replacement for `print()` with rich markup formatting.\n- `rich.inspect`: Introspective object visualizer.\n- `rich.get_console()`: Global default `Console` instance accessor.\n- `rich.traceback.install()`: Installs Rich exception handler for formatted stack traces.\n\n## Testing & Verification\n\n- Test command: `pytest tests/`\n\n## Architecture Notes\n\n- Follows the Rich Console Protocol (`__rich__` and `__rich_console__`).\n- Renders to atomic `Segment` instances before emitting ANSI escape sequences or Win32 calls.\n- Supports degradation/fallbacks for terminals without 24-bit TrueColor or Windows legacy console environments.\n\n## Related KIs\n\n- [[KI_rich_align.md]]\n- [[KI_rich_region.md]]\n- [[KI_rich_syntax.md]]\n- [[KI_rich_markdown.md]]\n- [[KI_rich_default.md]]\n- [[KI_rich_live.md]]\n- [[KI_rich_emoji.md]]\n- [[KI_rich_null.md]]\n- [[KI_rich_unicode11-0-0.md]]\n- [[KI_rich_unicode5-0-0.md]]\n<!-- last_verified: 2026-11-08 -->\n# KI: Rich Core (Internal Utilities & Platform Adaptors)\n\n## Overview\nProvides internal mathematical routines, layout ratio solvers, text wrapping primitives, platform Win32 console structures, and base ABC protocols. It forms the low-level foundation for rendering algorithms.\n\n## Entry Points & Public API\n- `ratio_resolve`: Integer ratio distribution algorithm for flex-like sizing in layouts and tables.\n- `words`: Word wrapping generator yielding split text positions without breaking ANSI tokens.\n- `RichRenderable`: Abstract base class enforcing the `__rich__` rendering protocol.\n- `NullFile`: Dummy writable file descriptor discarding all output.\n\n## Key Components\n| Class / Function | File | Purpose |\n|---|---|---|\n| `ratio_resolve` | `rich/_ratio.py` | Distributes integer space across items according to ratios and constraints |\n| `words` / `divide_line` | `rich/_wrap.py` | Word and character wrapping algorithms respecting cell widths and unicode boundaries |\n| `NullFile` | `rich/_null_file.py` | In-memory dummy stream implementing file protocol methods as no-ops |\n| `Stack` | `rich/_stack.py` | Lightweight wrapper over list providing stack operations with peak inspection |\n| `LegacyWindowsError` / Win32 structs | `rich/_win32_console.py` | ctypes definitions for Win32 Console API handles, buffers, and coordinates |\n| `RichRenderable` | `rich/abc.py` | Abstract base class verifying presence of `__rich__` magic method |\n| `SPINNERS` | `rich/_spinners.py` | Static catalog of animated spinner frame definitions and refresh intervals |\n\n## Testing & Verification\n- Test commands: `pytest tests/test_ratio.py tests/test_null_file.py tests/test_win32_console.py`\n- Test files: `tests/test_ratio.py`, `tests/test_null_file.py`, `tests/test_win32_console.py`\n\n## Non-obvious Details\n- **Integer ratio distribution rounding**: `ratio_resolve` distributes remainder pixels based on largest fractional residuals to ensure sum of parts exactly equals total width.\n- **NullFile compatibility**: Some 3rd-party libraries verify `.isatty()` or `.fileno()`; `NullFile` overrides these to gracefully avoid `io.UnsupportedOperation`.\nfrom typing import TYPE_CHECKING\n\nfrom .measure import Measurement\nfrom .segment import Segment\nfrom .style import StyleType\n\nif TYPE_CHECKING:\n    from .console import Console, ConsoleOptions, RenderResult, RenderableType\n\n\nclass Styled:\n    \"\"\"Apply a style to a renderable.\n\n    Args:\n        renderable (RenderableType): Any renderable.\n        style (StyleType): A style to apply across the entire renderable.\n    \"\"\"\n\n    def __init__(self, renderable: \"RenderableType\", style: \"StyleType\") -> None:\n        self.renderable = renderable\n        self.style = style\n\n    def __rich_console__(\n        self, console: \"Console\", options: \"ConsoleOptions\"\n    ) -> \"RenderResult\":\n        style = console.get_style(self.style)\n        rendered_segments = console.render(self.renderable, options)\n        segments = Segment.apply_style(rendered_segments, style)\n        return segments\n\n    def __rich_measure__(\n        self, console: \"Console\", options: \"ConsoleOptions\"\n    ) -> Measurement:\n        return Measurement.get(console, options, self.renderable)\n\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":  # pragma: no cover\n    from rich import print\n    from rich.panel import Panel\n\n    panel = Styled(Panel(\"hello\"), \"on blue\")\n    print(panel)\n"}],"structuredContent":{"output":"<!-- last_verified: 2026-11-08 -->\n# _OVERVIEW — Project Overview\n\n**Module**: `rich` (entire project)\n**Last verified**: 2026-11-08\n\n## Overview\n\nRich is a Python library for rendering rich text, tables, syntax highlighting, markdown, progress bars, and formatted data to terminal output and HTML. It serves as the primary rendering engine across console applications to provide modern CLI UX.\n\n## Subsystems & Knowledge Architecture\n\nThe codebase is partitioned into cohesive Knowledge Items (max 10 files per item):\n\n- [[KI_rich_align.md]]: Central `Console` orchestrator, ANSI escape parsing, cells width measurement, borders, and column layouts.\n- [[KI_rich_region.md]]: Low-level rendering primitives: `Segment`, `Style`, `Rule`, `Status`, `Spinner`, and screen switching.\n- [[KI_rich_syntax.md]]: Data presentation components: `Table`, `Text`, `Syntax`, `Traceback`, `Tree`, and `Theme`.\n- [[KI_rich_markdown.md]]: Markdown AST rendering, console `[markup]`, `Panel`, `Pretty` printing, and `Prompt` inputs.\n- [[KI_rich_default.md]]: Proportional multi-pane `Layout`, regex `Highlighter`, `RichHandler` logging, and JSON formatting.\n- [[KI_rich_live.md]]: Dynamic terminal updating (`Live`), multi-task progress meters (`Progress`), and IPython shims.\n- [[KI_rich_emoji.md]]: Emoji parsing, `Color` color models (Standard/256/Truecolor), and Windows console backends.\n- [[KI_rich_null.md]]: Internal ratio math, text wrapping routines, and Win32 low-level structures.\n- [[KI_rich_unicode11-0-0.md]] & [[KI_rich_unicode5-0-0.md]]: Unicode East Asian character width lookup tables.\n\n## Entry Points & Public API\n\n- `rich.print`: Direct drop-in replacement for `print()` with rich markup formatting.\n- `rich.inspect`: Introspective object visualizer.\n- `rich.get_console()`: Global default `Console` instance accessor.\n- `rich.traceback.install()`: Installs Rich exception handler for formatted stack traces.\n\n## Testing & Verification\n\n- Test command: `pytest tests/`\n\n## Architecture Notes\n\n- Follows the Rich Console Protocol (`__rich__` and `__rich_console__`).\n- Renders to atomic `Segment` instances before emitting ANSI escape sequences or Win32 calls.\n- Supports degradation/fallbacks for terminals without 24-bit TrueColor or Windows legacy console environments.\n\n## Related KIs\n\n- [[KI_rich_align.md]]\n- [[KI_rich_region.md]]\n- [[KI_rich_syntax.md]]\n- [[KI_rich_markdown.md]]\n- [[KI_rich_default.md]]\n- [[KI_rich_live.md]]\n- [[KI_rich_emoji.md]]\n- [[KI_rich_null.md]]\n- [[KI_rich_unicode11-0-0.md]]\n- [[KI_rich_unicode5-0-0.md]]\n<!-- last_verified: 2026-11-08 -->\n# KI: Rich Core (Internal Utilities & Platform Adaptors)\n\n## Overview\nProvides internal mathematical routines, layout ratio solvers, text wrapping primitives, platform Win32 console structures, and base ABC protocols. It forms the low-level foundation for rendering algorithms.\n\n## Entry Points & Public API\n- `ratio_resolve`: Integer ratio distribution algorithm for flex-like sizing in layouts and tables.\n- `words`: Word wrapping generator yielding split text positions without breaking ANSI tokens.\n- `RichRenderable`: Abstract base class enforcing the `__rich__` rendering protocol.\n- `NullFile`: Dummy writable file descriptor discarding all output.\n\n## Key Components\n| Class / Function | File | Purpose |\n|---|---|---|\n| `ratio_resolve` | `rich/_ratio.py` | Distributes integer space across items according to ratios and constraints |\n| `words` / `divide_line` | `rich/_wrap.py` | Word and character wrapping algorithms respecting cell widths and unicode boundaries |\n| `NullFile` | `rich/_null_file.py` | In-memory dummy stream implementing file protocol methods as no-ops |\n| `Stack` | `rich/_stack.py` | Lightweight wrapper over list providing stack operations with peak inspection |\n| `LegacyWindowsError` / Win32 structs | `rich/_win32_console.py` | ctypes definitions for Win32 Console API handles, buffers, and coordinates |\n| `RichRenderable` | `rich/abc.py` | Abstract base class verifying presence of `__rich__` magic method |\n| `SPINNERS` | `rich/_spinners.py` | Static catalog of animated spinner frame definitions and refresh intervals |\n\n## Testing & Verification\n- Test commands: `pytest tests/test_ratio.py tests/test_null_file.py tests/test_win32_console.py`\n- Test files: `tests/test_ratio.py`, `tests/test_null_file.py`, `tests/test_win32_console.py`\n\n## Non-obvious Details\n- **Integer ratio distribution rounding**: `ratio_resolve` distributes remainder pixels based on largest fractional residuals to ensure sum of parts exactly equals total width.\n- **NullFile compatibility**: Some 3rd-party libraries verify `.isatty()` or `.fileno()`; `NullFile` overrides these to gracefully avoid `io.UnsupportedOperation`.\nfrom typing import TYPE_CHECKING\n\nfrom .measure import Measurement\nfrom .segment import Segment\nfrom .style import StyleType\n\nif TYPE_CHECKING:\n    from .console import Console, ConsoleOptions, RenderResult, RenderableType\n\n\nclass Styled:\n    \"\"\"Apply a style to a renderable.\n\n    Args:\n        renderable (RenderableType): Any renderable.\n        style (StyleType): A style to apply across the entire renderable.\n    \"\"\"\n\n    def __init__(self, renderable: \"RenderableType\", style: \"StyleType\") -> None:\n        self.renderable = renderable\n        self.style = style\n\n    def __rich_console__(\n        self, console: \"Console\", options: \"ConsoleOptions\"\n    ) -> \"RenderResult\":\n        style = console.get_style(self.style)\n        rendered_segments = console.render(self.renderable, options)\n        segments = Segment.apply_style(rendered_segments, style)\n        return segments\n\n    def __rich_measure__(\n        self, console: \"Console\", options: \"ConsoleOptions\"\n    ) -> Measurement:\n        return Measurement.get(console, options, self.renderable)\n\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":  # pragma: no cover\n    from rich import print\n    from rich.panel import Panel\n\n    panel = Styled(Panel(\"hello\"), \"on blue\")\n    print(panel)\n","truncated":false,"exit_code":0,"wall_time_seconds":0.1}},"isError":false,"durationMs":112}
