files*\n```\n\n## Key Directory Purposes\n\n| Directory | Purpose |\n|---|---|\n| `.ki-base/` | Knowledge system: KI files, workflows, scripts |\n| `.ki-base/knowledge/` | KI files for AI agents |\n| `.ki-base/decisions/` | Architectural Decision Records (ADR) |\n\n---\n*Generated by: `.ki-base/scripts/generate_dir_index.py`*\n<!-- last_verified: 2026-11-08 -->\n# KI: Rich Core (Layouts, Highlighters & Logging)\n\n## Overview\nHouses split-screen terminal layout panes (`Layout`), pattern regex highlighters (`Highlighter`), JSON syntax formatters, Rich logging handlers (`RichHandler`), default theme color rules, and Jupyter notebook rendering shims.\nfrom typing import Optional, TYPE_CHECKING\n\nfrom .jupyter import JupyterMixin\nfrom .measure import Measurement\n\nif TYPE_CHECKING:\n    from .console import Console, ConsoleOptions, RenderableType, RenderResult\n\n\nclass Constrain(JupyterMixin):\n    \"\"\"Constrain the width of a renderable to a given number of characters.\n\n    Args:\n        renderable (RenderableType): A renderable object.\n        width (int, optional): The maximum width (in characters) to render. Defaults to 80.\n    \"\"\"\n\n    def __init__(self, renderable: \"RenderableType\", width: Optional[int] = 80) -> None:\n        self.renderable = renderable\n        self.width = width\n\n    def __rich_console__(\n        self, console: \"Console\", options: \"ConsoleOptions\"\n    ) -> \"RenderResult\":\n        if self.width is None:\n            yield self.renderable\n        else:\n            child_options = options.update_width(min(self.width, options.max_width))\n            yield from console.render(self.renderable, child_options)\n\n    def __rich_measure__(\n        self, console: \"Console\", options: \"ConsoleOptions\"\n    ) -> \"Measurement\":\n        if self.width is not None:\n            options = options.update_width(self.width)\n        measurement = Measurement.get(console, options, self.renderable)\n        return measurement\nrich/__init__.py:8:__all__ = [\"get_console\", \"reconfigure\", \"print\", \"inspect\", \"print_json\"]\nrich/__main__.py:33:    def __rich_measure__(\nrich/align.py:235:    def __rich_measure__(\nrich/align.py:292:    def __rich_measure__(\nrich/bar.py:86:    def __rich_measure__(\nrich/console.py:468:    def __rich_measure__(\nrich/constrain.py:31:    def __rich_measure__(\nrich/containers.py:46:    def __rich_measure__(\nrich/filesize.py:13:__all__ = [\"decimal\"]\nrich/measure.py:106:            ] = getattr(renderable, \"__rich_measure__\", None)\nrich/padding.py:125:    def __rich_measure__(\nrich/panel.py:277:    def __rich_measure__(\nrich/pretty.py:339:    def __rich_measure__(\nrich/progress_bar.py:200:    def __rich_measure__(\nrich/rule.py:111:    def __rich_measure__(\nrich/spinner.py:55:    def __rich_measure__(\nrich/styled.py:31:    def __rich_measure__(\nrich/syntax.py:625:    def __rich_measure__(\nrich/table.py:320:    def __rich_measure__(\nrich/text.py:707:    def __rich_measure__(\nrich/tree.py:176:    def __rich_measure__(\n/bin/bash: line 1: python: command not found\n\n\nCommand exited with code 127"}],"isError":true,"durationMs":1359,"timestamp":1794167837583},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The ADR directory .ki-base/decisions shows as deleted in the git working tree, so I want to see whether it still exists in HEAD. I'll check the committed tree for that path.\n\n","thinkingSignature":".eyJlbmRwb2ludF9zbHVnIjoiYW50aHJvcGljL2NsYXVkZS1oYWlrdS01LjUtMjAyNjEwMDd8Y2xhdWRlLW9uLWF3cyJ9"},{"type":"text","text":"The ADRs should live in `.ki-base/decisions/`, which is among the deleted files. I'll check whether they exist in git history, and find the Python interpreter."},{"type":"toolCall","id":"toolu_01HLpJXD371cxiVivN7dPoMX","name":"bash","arguments":{"command":"cd /app && git ls-files .ki-base | head -30; git show HEAD --stat -- .ki-base | head -5; git log --oneline -3; for f in $(git ls-files .ki-base/decisions);