nking","thinking":"No decisions directory turns up in git, so there are no ADRs to draw on. I'll make a note of that. Before going further, I want to see whether the overview file sets out conventions, so I'll read the top of the overview and search it for \"badge\" or \"protocol\".\n\n","thinkingSignature":".eyJlbmRwb2ludF9zbHVnIjoiYW50aHJvcGljL2NsYXVkZS1oYWlrdS01LjUtMjAyNjEwMDd8Y2xhdWRlLW9uLWF3cyJ9"},{"type":"text","text":"No `decisions/` ADRs exist in git history, so I'll check the knowledge base overview for the conventions, then look at a small existing renderable to model on."},{"type":"toolCall","id":"toolu_01J8AfxJe9YThyBWN4Jreaxd","name":"bash","arguments":{"command":"cd /app && git show HEAD:.ki-base/knowledge/_OVERVIEW.ki.md | head -80; git show HEAD:.ki-base/knowledge/KI_rich_null.md | head -30; sed -n 1,60p rich/styled.py"}}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"openrouter","model":"anthropic/claude-haiku-5.5","usage":{"input":2,"output":311,"cacheRead":9688,"cacheWrite":880,"totalTokens":10881,"cost":{"input":2.0000000000000002e-7,"output":0.00015549999999999999,"cacheRead":0.00009688000000000001,"cacheWrite":0.00011,"total":0.00036258,"totalFromProvider":true},"cacheWrite1h":0,"reasoning":126},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1794167839543,"providerThinkingLevel":"medium","responseId":"msg_011Cgr3vYSqj6AL9EphYvqYC","rawStopReason":"tool_use","durationMs":1958,"thinkingLevel":"medium"},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"toolu_01J8AfxJe9YThyBWN4Jreaxd","toolName":"bash","content":[{"type":"text","text":"<!-- last_verified: 2026-11-08 -->\n# _OVERVIEW — Project Overview\n\n**Module**: `rich` (entire project)\n**Last verified**: 2026-11-08\n\n## Overview\n\nRich is a Python library for rendering rich text, tables, syntax highlighting, markdown, progress bars, and formatted data to terminal output and HTML. It serves as the primary rendering engine across console applications to provide modern CLI UX.\n\n## Subsystems & Knowledge Architecture\n\nThe codebase is partitioned into cohesive Knowledge Items (max 10 files per item):\n\n- [[KI_rich_align.md]]: Central `Console` orchestrator, ANSI escape parsing, cells width measurement, borders, and column layouts.\n- [[KI_rich_region.md]]: Low-level rendering primitives: `Segment`, `Style`, `Rule`, `Status`, `Spinner`, and screen switching.\n- [[KI_rich_syntax.md]]: Data presentation components: `Table`, `Text`, `Syntax`, `Traceback`, `Tree`, and `Theme`.\n- [[KI_rich_markdown.md]]: Markdown AST rendering, console `[markup]`, `Panel`, `Pretty` printing, and `Prompt` inputs.\n- [[KI_rich_default.md]]: Proportional multi-pane `Layout`, regex `Highlighter`, `RichHandler` logging, and JSON formatting.\n- [[KI_rich_live.md]]: Dynamic terminal updating (`Live`), multi-task progress meters (`Progress`), and IPython shims.\n- [[KI_rich_emoji.md]]: Emoji parsing, `Color` color models (Standard/256/Truecolor), and Windows console backends.\n- [[KI_rich_null.md]]: Internal ratio math, text wrapping routines, and Win32 low-level structures.\n- [[KI_rich_unicode11-0-0.md]] & [[KI_rich_unicode5-0-0.md]]: Unicode East Asian character width lookup tables.\n\n## Entry Points & Public API\n\n- `rich.print`: Direct drop-in replacement for `print()` with rich markup formatting.\n- `rich.inspect`: Introspective object visualizer.\n- `rich.get_console()`: Global default `Console` instance accessor.\n- `rich.traceback.install()`: Installs Rich exception handler for formatted stack traces.\n\n## Testing & Verification\n\n- Test command: `pytest tests/`\n\n## Architecture Notes\n\n- Follows the Rich Console Protocol (`__rich__` and `__rich_console__`).\n- Renders to atomic `Segment` instances before emitting ANSI escape sequences or Win32 calls.\n- Supports degradation/fallbacks for terminals without 24-bit TrueColor or Windows legacy console environments.\n\n## Related KIs\n\n- [[KI_rich_align.md]]\n- [[KI_rich_region.md]]\n- [[KI_rich_syntax.md]]\n- [[KI_rich_markdown.md]]\n- [[KI_rich_default.md]]\n- [[KI_rich_live.md]]\n- [[KI_rich_emoji.md]]\n- [[KI_rich_null.md]]\n- [[KI_rich_unicode11-0-0.md]]\n- [[KI_rich_unicode5-0-0.md]]\n<!-- last_verified: 2026-11-08 -->\n# KI: Rich Core (Internal Utilities & Platform Adaptors)\n\n## Overview\nProvides internal mathematical routines, layout ratio solvers, text wrapping primitives, platform Win32 console structures, and base ABC protocols. It forms the low-level foundation for rendering algorithms.\n\n## Entry Points & Public API\n- `ratio_resolve`: Integer ratio distribution algorithm for flex-like sizing in layouts and tables.\n- `words`: Word wrapping generator yielding split text positions without breaking ANSI tokens.\n- `RichRenderable`: Abstract base class enforcing the `__rich__` rendering protocol.\n- `NullFile`: Dummy writable file descriptor discarding all output.\n\n## Key Components\n| Class / Function | File | Purpose |\n|---|---|---|\n| `ratio_resolve` | `rich/_ratio.py` | Distributes integer space across items according to ratios and constraints |\n| `words` / `divide_line` | `rich/_wrap.py` | Word and character wrapping algorithms respecting cell widths and unicode boundaries |\n| `NullFile` | `rich/_null_file.py` | In-memory dummy stream implementing file protocol methods as no-ops |\n| `Stack` | `rich/_stack.py` | Lightweight wrapper over list providing stack operations with peak inspection |\n| `LegacyWindowsError` / Win32 structs | `rich/_win32_console.py` | ctypes definitions for Win32 Console API handles, buffers, and coordinates |\n| `RichRenderable` | `rich/abc.py` | Abstract base class verifying presence of `__rich__` magic method |\n| `SPINNERS` | `rich/_spinners.py` | Static catalog of animated spinner frame definitions and refresh intervals |\n\n## Testing & Verification\n- Test commands: `pytest tests/test_ratio.py tests/test_null_file.py tests/test_win32_console.py`\n- Test files: `tests/test_ratio.py`, `tests/test_null_file.py`, `tests/test_win32_console.py`\n\n## Non-obvious Details\n- **Integer ratio distribution rounding**: `ratio_resolve` distributes remainder pixels based on largest fractional residuals to ensure sum of parts exactly equals total width.\n- **NullFile compatibility**: Some 3rd-party libraries verify `.isatty()` or `.fileno()`; `NullFile` overrides these to gracefully avoid `io.UnsupportedOperation`.\nfrom typing import TYPE_CHECKING\n\nfrom .measure import Measurement\nfrom .segment import Segment\nfrom .style import StyleType\n\nif TYPE_CHECKING:\n    from .console import Console, ConsoleOptions, RenderResult, RenderableType\n\n\nclass Styled:\n    \"\"\"Apply a style to a renderable.\n\n    Args:\n        renderable (RenderableType): Any renderable.\n        style (StyleType): A style to apply across the entire renderable.\n    \"\"\"\n\n    def __init__(self, renderable: \"RenderableType\", style: \"StyleType\") -> None:\n        self.renderable = renderable\n        self.style = style\n\n    def __rich_console__(\n        self, console: \"Console\", options: \"ConsoleOptions\"\n    ) -> \"RenderResult\":\n        style = console.get_style(self.style)\n        rendered_segments = console.render(self.renderable, options)\n        segments = Segment.apply_style(rendered_segments, style)\n        return segments\n\n    def __rich_measure__(\n        self, console: \"Console\", options: \"ConsoleOptions\"\n    ) -> Measurement:\n        return Measurement.get(console, options, self.renderable)\n\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":  # pragma: no cover\n    from rich import print\n    from rich.panel import Panel\n\n    panel = Styled(Panel(\"hello\"), \"on blue\")\n    print(panel)\n"}],"isError":false,"durationMs":112,"timestamp":1794167841616},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"I'm checking for the ADRs, which turn out to be absent, so I'll follow the repo's usual conventions: a `__rich_console__` generator that yields Segments, a `__rich_measure__` that returns a Measurement, `cell_len` for width, and no touching `console._buffer`. I'm weighing whether to build a Text object and render it, but I'd rather yield Segments directly and truncate them to `options.max_width`.\n\nI'm settling on the badge layout now: the content gets wrapped in \"( \" and \" )\" for pill borders and \"[ \" and \" ]\" for square ones. I'm leaning toward building a Text object with styled spans and rendering it through the console, so wrapping and cell width are handled for me, rather than hand-cropping raw Segments.\n\nI'm sizing the badge by adding up the cell widths of the left border, content, and right border, then returning a fixed Measurement and letting the caller clamp it to the available width. I'm also planning to make the Text non-wrapping with ellipsis overflow so it stays on one line and crops cleanly when space is tight.\n\nI'm checking the ordering of Text.assemble parts, which takes (str, style) pairs, and that style strings get resolved at render time through the console, so they can stay as plain strings. I'm also deciding whether Badge should inherit JupyterMixin like Constrain does, and I'm leaning toward including it for consistency.\n\nI'm working out how to export Badge from the top-level rich package without causing import trouble, since the new module pulls in text handling. I'm checking whether rich.text leads back into rich.console, which would decide whether a top-level import is safe or needs to be deferred.\n\nI'm checking how `rich/__init__.py` pulls in its other modules so I can add `Badge` to the top-level imports, and I'll run an import test afterward to make sure there's no circularity. I'm also planning to extend `__all__` with \"Badge\" and to add a small test module alongside the component.\n\n","thinkingSignature":".eyJlbmRwb2ludF9zbHVnIjoiYW50aHJvcGljL2NsYXVkZS1oYWlrdS01LjUtMjAyNjEwMDd8Y2xhdWRlLW9uLWF3cyJ9"},{"type":"text","text":"I couldn't find the ADRs: `.ki-base/decisions/` is not in git history. The knowledge base does state the conventions I'll follow: `__rich_console__` yields `Segment`s or nested renderables, `__rich_measure__` returns a `Measurement`, and no private console buffers. I'll check the `Text`/`Measurement` APIs I plan to use, and whether `rich/text.py` imports cleanly from the package root."},{"type":"toolCall","id":"toolu_01UoG2WTbdH1y5bvmBywbbQ1","name":"bash","arguments":{"command":"cd /app && grep -n \"^from\\|^import\" rich/text.py rich/measure.py rich/jupyter.py | head -30; grep -n \"def assemble\\|def __init__\" rich/text.py | head; grep -n \"def get\\b\" -A12 rich/measure.py | head -30"}}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"openrouter","model":"anthropic/claude-haiku-5.5","usage":{"input":2,"output":1861,"cacheRead":10568,"cacheWrite":2784,"totalTokens":15215,"cost":{"input":2.0000000000000002e-7,"output":0.0009305,"cacheRead":0.00010568,"cacheWrite":0.000348,"total":0.00138438,"totalFromProvider":true},"cacheWrite1h":0,"reasoning":1576},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1794167841620,"providerThinkingLevel":"medium","responseId":"msg_011Cgr3vhJesVddVDLCrkht2","rawStopReason":"tool_use","durationMs":8986,"thinkingLevel":"medium"},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"toolu_01UoG2WTbdH1y5bvmBywbbQ1","toolName":"bash","content":[{"type":"text","text":"rich/text.py:1:import re\nrich/text.py:2:from functools import partial, reduce\nrich/text.py:3:from math import gcd\nrich/text.py:4:from operator import itemgetter\nrich/text.py:5:from typing import (\nrich/text.py:19:from ._loop import loop_last\nrich/text.py:20:from ._pick import pick_bool\nrich/text.py:21:from ._wrap import divide_line\nrich/text.py:22:from .align import AlignMethod\nrich/text.py:23:from .cells import cell_len, set_cell_size\nrich/text.py:24:from .containers import Lines\nrich/text.py:25:from .control import strip_control_codes\nrich/text.py:26:from .emoji import EmojiVariant\nrich/text.py:27:from .jupyter import JupyterMixin\nrich/text.py:28:from .measure import Measurement\nrich/text.py:29:from .segment import Segment\nrich/text.py:30:from .style import Style, StyleType\nrich/measure.py:1:from operator import itemgetter\nrich/measure.py:2:from typing import TYPE_CHECKING, Callable, NamedTuple, Optional, Sequence\nrich/measure.py:4:from . import errors\nrich/measure.py:5:from .protocol import is_renderable, rich_cast\nrich/jupyter.py:1:from typing import TYPE_CHECKING, Any, Dict, Iterable, List, Sequence\nrich/jupyter.py:6:from . import get_console\nrich/jupyter.py:7:from .segment import Segment\nrich/jupyter.py:8:from .terminal_theme import DEFAULT_TERMINAL_THEME\n144:    def __init__(\n357:    def assemble(\n79:    def get(\n80-        cls, console: \"Console\", options: \"ConsoleOptions\", renderable: \"RenderableType\"\n81-    ) -> \"Measurement\":\n82-        \"\"\"Get a measurement for a renderable.\n83-\n84-        Args:\n85-            console (~rich.console.Console): Console instance.\n86-            options (~rich.console.ConsoleOptions): Console options.\n87-            renderable (RenderableType): An object that may be rendered with Rich.\n88-\n89-        Raises:\n90-            errors.NotRenderableError: If the object is not renderable.\n91-\n"}],"isError":false,"durationMs":17,"timestamp":1794167850626},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"I'm planning badge.py around Text.assemble with no_wrap and ellipsis overflow, leaning on Text's default end=\"\\n\". I still need to check how the base style behaves when nested inside Columns, and how Text's measurement handles the icon and spaces so the width stays fixed.\n\nI'll work out the total width directly, since the minimum and maximum measurements won't give me the fixed width I need for the badge.\n\n","thinkingSignature":".eyJlbmRwb2ludF9zbHVnIjoiYW50aHJvcGljL2NsYXVkZS1oYWlrdS01LjUtMjAyNjEwMDd8Y2xhdWRlLW9uLWF3cyJ9"},{"type":"text","text":"The plan: build a single `Text` with styled spans and `no_wrap`/`ellipsis`, so the badge stays on one line and gets cropped rather than broken when space is tight. Measurement is the exact cell width, which `Measurement.get` clamps to `max_width` for nested layouts."},{"type":"toolCall","id":"toolu_01VSZVEyBchhiyF4jQwDDZP9","name":"write","arguments":{"path":"/app/rich/badge.py","content":"from typing import TYPE_CHECKING, Optional\n\nfrom .cells import cell_len\nfrom .jupyter import JupyterMixin\nfrom .measure import Measurement\nfrom .style import StyleType\nfrom .text import Text\n\nif TYPE_CHECKING:\n    from .console import Console, ConsoleOptions, RenderResult\n\n\nclass Badge(JupyterMixin):\n    \"\"\"A single-line status badge, e.g. ``( ✔ passed )``.\n\n    Args:\n        text (str): The badge label.\n        style (StyleType, optional): Style applied to the label. Defaults to \"bold white on blue\".\n        border_style (StyleType, optional): Style applied to the border characters. Defaults to \"blue\".\n        pill (bool, optional): Use curved pill borders ``( ... )`` if True, or square\n            borders ``[ ... ]`` if False. Defaults to True.\n        icon (str, optional): An optional icon rendered before the label, separated by a space. Defaults to None.\n    \"\"\"\n\n    def __init__(\n        self,\n        text: str,\n        *,\n        style: StyleType = \"bold white on blue\",\n        border_style: StyleType = \"blue\",\n        pill: bool = True,\n        icon: Optional[str] = None,\n    ) -> None:\n        self.text = text\n        self.style = style\n        self.border_style = border_style\n        self.pill = pill\n        self.icon = icon\n\n    @property\n    def _left_border(self) -> str:\n        return \"( \" if self.pill else \"[ \"\n\n    @property\n    def _right_border(self) -> str:\n        return \" )\" if self.pill else \" ]\"\n\n    @property\n    def _label(self) -> str:\n        return f\"{self.icon} {self.text}\" if self.icon else self.text\n\n    def __rich_console__(\n        self, console: \"Console\", options: \"ConsoleOptions\"\n    ) -> \"RenderResult\":\n        badge = Text.assemble(\n            (self._left_border, self.border_style),\n            (self._label, self.style),\n            (self._right_border, self.border_style),\n            no_wrap=True,\n            overflow=\"ellipsis\",\n        )\n        yield from console.render(badge, options)\n\n    def __rich_measure__(\n        self, console: \"Console\", options: \"ConsoleOptions\"\n    ) -> Measurement:\n        # The badge never wraps, so its minimum and maximum widths are both the full cell width.\n        width = cell_len(self._left_border + self._label + self._right_border)\n        return Measurement(width, width)\n\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":  # pragma: no cover\n    from rich import print\n\n    print(Badge(\"passed\", icon=\"✔\", style=\"bold white on green\", border_style=\"green\"))\n    print(Badge(\"v1.2.0\", pill=False, style=\"bold yellow\", border_style=\"yellow\"))\n"}}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"openrouter","model":"anthropic/claude-haiku-5.5","usage":{"input":2,"output":1240,"cacheRead":13352,"cacheWrite":2646,"totalTokens":17240,"cost":{"input":2.0000000000000002e-7,"output":0.00062,"cacheRead":0.00013352,"cacheWrite":0.00033075,"total":0.00108447,"totalFromProvider":true},"cacheWrite1h":0,"reasoning":163},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1794167850630,"providerThinkingLevel":"medium","responseId":"msg_011Cgr3wMpefdTsuQVKUaJqw","rawStopReason":"tool_use","durationMs":5043,"thinkingLevel":"medium"},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"toolu_01VSZVEyBchhiyF4jQwDDZP9","toolName":"write","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Successfully wrote to /app/rich/badge.py"}],"isError":false,"durationMs":6,"timestamp":1794167855683},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"I'm checking the signature of `Text.assemble`, which takes `no_wrap` and `overflow` among its keyword arguments, and it matches what I expected. Next I'll move on to `__init__`.\n\n","thinkingSignature":".eyJlbmRwb2ludF9zbHVnIjoiYW50aHJvcGljL2N